ChannelTerm Electron is licensed under the repository's Apache License 2.0.

The independent npm dependency graph is pinned in package-lock.json. The current
installed JavaScript dependency notices include MIT, ISC, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, and Apache-2.0
licenses. Electron uses MIT and includes Chromium and other third-party code
with their own notices.

Menu localization uses Lingui Core 5.9.0 (MIT). Its installed dependency licenses
are included by the same notice collection; no translation service is contacted.
The matching Lingui CLI/config/PO tools are build dependencies, not application
services. npm may also install optional build-tool peers; their installed notices
are retained conservatively. Absent optional packages for other platforms are skipped;
missing required packages or license texts in installed packages remain build errors.

npm run build collects the installed runtime dependency license texts, including
the Electron npm package license, into dist/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt and copies the
ChannelTerm license into dist/LICENSE. Redistribution of the bundled JavaScript
must retain those files. The generated notices cover the installed production
dependency graph, including packages that the client bundle may not use.

A future desktop package must additionally retain Electron's distributed LICENSE
and LICENSES.chromium.html and any accompanying runtime notices, and include the
repository THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES when bundling a Go Host. This prototype does not
produce an installer or redistribute an Electron runtime archive.
